+// The same alert, built out of the dialog's own buttons rather than a list the
+// caller assembles: every one of Orca's Button widgets that is a direct child
+// of `dlg` becomes a row, in the order they were created.
+//
+// For the dialogs here that are a sentence and some buttons but are not
+// MsgDialogs - there are several, because MsgDialog is not the only base a
+// message in this application ever got written on, and each of them would
+// otherwise need the same twenty lines.
+//
+// An empty `message` means "the text is in the dialog", and the static text it
+// holds is read out and joined in child order. These dialogs typically build a
+// Label in the constructor, hand it to a sizer and keep no pointer to it, so
+// the control is the only place the sentence still exists.
+//
+// Returns false, having shown nothing, when the dialog holds no button to make
+// a row out of or the alert cannot be presented. The caller then shows its
+// window, exactly as with orca_ios_alert_run().
+bool orca_ios_alert_from_buttons(wxDialog       *dlg,
+                                 const wxString &title,
+                                 const wxString &message,
+                                 int            *result);
+
